    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2010.15116_rag::chunk_000</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2005.12386_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2009.00934_rag::chunk_016</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2009.00934_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">graph neural networks (GNNs) have received much more attention and are devel</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Modern GNNs typically adopt a neighborhood aggregation strategy by using 2322 the features and graph structures to learn discriminative node or graph representations.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">much effort has been devoted to generalizing neural networks to graph-structured data, resulting in the development of graph neural networks (GNNs).</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">As a powerful tool of learning on graph-structured data, Graph Neural Networks</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are the rst choice methods for graph machine learning problems thanks to their ability to learn state-of-the-art level representations from graph-structured data.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) have demonstrated superior performance in learning node representations for various graph inference tasks.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Different from CNNs handling grid data, GNNs can take nongird data as inputs. A non-grid data can be represented as a graph G = { V, E }</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">leveraging a Graph Neural Network (GNN) based model to capture the spatial relationship among clients.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Modern graph neural networks (GNNs) learn node embeddings through multilayer local aggregation</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), which can learn effective representations from irregular data, have given excellent performances in various graphbased tasks</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are an effective framework for representation learning of graphs. GNNs follow a neighborhood aggregation scheme</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">graph neural networks (GNNs) [Kipf and Welling, 2017] that explicitly deal with the topological structures of these graph data.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">we propose a novel distributed algorithm for training Graph Neural Networks (GNNs).</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are popular for graph machine learning and have shown great results on wide node classication tasks.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">enhancing the training of graph neural networks (GNNs)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A graph neural network model usually consists of several GNN layers, where each layer takes the output of the previous layer as the input.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">graph convolutional network (GCN) to learn node and graph representations</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), which can learn effective representations from irregular data</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">multi-layer Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">modeling rich relation information among samples, graph neural networks (GNNs) have received much more attention</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Any existing graph neural network model can be adapted by the Customized-GNN framework to generate sample-specic models based on the structure information.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Despite the recent success of Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), training GNNs on large graphs remains challenging.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Selfsupervised learning of graph neural networks</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">representations with graph neural networks (GNNs) for unsupervised scenario.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
