    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">only a small set of nodes are labeled</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">nodes with edge connection have similar node embeddings.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Transformer performs message propagation between all nodes and encodes the given graph structure as a soft inductive bias</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">there are two types of nodes, i.e., user node and item node</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The neighborhood N S is restricted to nodes which are immediate neighbors of the source.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">every node propagates its message to hops further</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">other node types like author, eld, venue</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">predictions of the nodes in the batch contribute to the loss computation</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">learned representations for the nodes in the same class</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">V is a set of | V | = n nodes and E V V is a set of | E | edges between nodes.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">represent nodes as high-dimensional feature vectors.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
